## Technical Outcome

The project resulted in an AWS SOAR architecture with two working response
patterns:

**IAM compromise**

GuardDuty / Security Hub  
→ EventBridge  
→ Step Functions  
→ enrichment  
→ notification  
→ credential containment  
→ escalation when required  
→ S3 execution artifact

**EC2 compromise**

GuardDuty / Security Hub  
→ EventBridge  
→ Step Functions  
→ enrichment  
→ notification  
→ snapshot initiation and network containment  
→ escalation when required  
→ S3 execution artifact

The project also exposed and corrected a lifecycle weakness in the supporting
audit architecture.

The main technical lesson was that security automation cannot be evaluated
only by whether the remediation code works.

The surrounding architecture — identity, orchestration, failure handling,
evidence, logging, lifecycle, cost, and human escalation — determines whether
the automation can operate safely and sustainably.
